  "instruction": "In the Odoo backend, go to the Sales app and create a NEW quotation (Sales > Orders > Quotations, click New). Set the Customer field to 'fwod50-n1 Bench Customer' — this is an autocomplete dropdown, so type the name and actually select the option from the dropdown list that appears (do not just type and leave it). Then add EXACTLY ONE order line: in the Order Lines notebook section, click 'Add a product', and in the product field of that single line pick ANY product from the catalogue (again via the autocomplete dropdown — select an actual option). Set that line's Quantity to 3. Do NOT add any second line. Let Odoo auto-fill the Unit Price and the Untaxed Amount. Then save the quotation. Report: (a) the product name you chose, (b) the Unit Price the app filled in for that line, (c) the Untaxed Amount the app computes, and (d) the quotation's reference/name (e.g. S00042) shown on the form. Do not wait for network idle (the app long-polls) — wait on concrete page state.",
